    The chapter opens at the top of printed 99 and the heading "The
    Cosmo-Knight O.C.C." is partway down printed 100; the entry''s last line is
    the Cybernetics line near the foot of the right column of printed 102, with
    "The Fallen Knights" heading below it on the same page. Printed 98, which
    is zero bytes in the OCR cache, was rendered and is a full-page
    illustration with the folio 98 printed on it - it splits this chapter from
    the Dominator and nothing of the entry is on it.
  - THE ATTRIBUTE LINE IS A TAKE-THE-HIGHER RULE AND THE APP CANNOT HOLD IT.
    The book says to use these die rolls OR the attributes of the character''s
    original race, whichever are HIGHER. `attribute_dice` holds one expression
    per attribute and `combineClasses` does not compare two of them: it gives
    the RACE precedence outright wherever the race states any. Measured on all
    57 published R.C.C.s - the cosmo-knight''s own dice survive on 3 of them,
    and only because those three state no dice at all. A kreeghor cosmo-knight
    rolls P.S. 3d6+10 where this class prints 3d6+32. The dice are stored
    anyway, because a character with no race at all then gets the printed
    figures and one omitting them would roll a flat 3d6 in every case. Filed as
    BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F11.
  - THE SAME FINDING TAKES THE M.D.C. AND THE P.P.E. `combineClasses` gives the
    race precedence on `mdc_base` and `ppe_base` too, so the transformed body
    this entry describes is discarded for a race that states its own: 36 of 57
    races drop the 4D6x10+60 and 50 of 57 drop the 1D6x100. And O.C.C. SKILLS
    SAYS THE PAST LIFE IS LOST AND THE CHARACTER IS REBORN, which
    `combineClasses` cannot express either - it UNIONS the two skill lists, so
    37 of 57 races carry between 1 and 19 named skills through a transformation
    the book says erases them. Exactly ONE race of 57 composes this class
    correctly in all four places, and only by stating nothing in any of them.
    All three are one finding, F11.
  - THE COSMIC ARMOR''S 500 M.D.C. IS NOT IN `mdc_base`. The M.D.C. line prints
    the body''s 4D6x10+60 plus 4D6 per level AND the armor''s additional 500 in
    one breath, and they are two different things: the armor is summoned, it is
    ability 6, and a fallen knight keeps half the body figure while losing the
    armor entirely. Storing 560 would give an unarmored knight the armor.
  - GALACTIC AWARENESS PRINTS TWO SKILL PERCENTAGES AND ONE OF THEM ARGUES WITH
    THE SKILL LIST. The O.C.C. Skills line grants Navigation: Space (+15%),
    which over the catalog base of 40 is 55%; the ability states an effective
    navigation: space skill of 89%. The higher, result-shaped figure is stored
    and the bonus-shaped one is recorded here. Land navigation at 92% has no
    competing entry and is granted outright - the catalog holds the row, which
    is the test for whether a percentage printed outside a skill list is a
    skill.
  - FOUR OF THE SEVEN SKILL NAMES ARE FILED IN THE CATALOG UNDER OTHER NAMES,
    and each was checked against the live catalog rather than assumed:
    Navigation: Space is `Navigation: Stellar`, Movement: Zero Gravity is
    `Space: Zero Gravity Movement & Combat`, Demon and Monster Lore is
    `Lore: Demons & Monsters`, and the three languages of choice resolve
    through the repeatable `Language: Other` row rather than through a
    category. Radio: Basic and Hand to Hand: Martial Arts are catalog names
    already.
  - THE BONUS LINE IS SAFE TO STORE AND ITS HEADING IS WHY. It reads "Bonuses"
    and closes with the statement that all of them are in addition to attribute
    and skill bonuses, so `derive.js` adding its own P.P. and P.S. figures on
    top is what the book intends. A line headed "Includes P.P. bonuses" would
    have had to be dropped; this one is not.
  - THE +4 SAVE IS PRINTED FOR TWO THINGS AND ONLY ONE HAS A FIELD. The book
    gives +4 to save vs mega-damage poisons AND vs bio-wizard microbes and
    parasites. `toxins_poisons` carries the first half exactly: the class is
    already impervious to S.D.C. poisons, so a poison save can only ever fire
    against the mega-damage kind the book names, and the widening is inert. The
    microbes and parasites have no field. `disease` was considered and rejected
    - a bio-wizard parasite is not a disease, the class is impervious to
    disease anyway, and a near-miss save that renders is worse than an absent
    one. See BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F7.
  - THE COSMIC BLAST''S +1 INITIATIVE AND +3 STRIKE ARE NOT IN `bonuses`. They
    belong to the blast, not to the knight, and `bonuses.combat` applies
    unconditionally - stored there they would improve every punch and every
    sword stroke. They are in the ability, which is where a conditional bonus
    goes.
  - NO `Money:` LINE AND NO EQUIPMENT LIST, AND THAT IS THE ENTRY''S OWN DOING.
    Grepped across printed 99 to 104: not one `Money:` line on either
    cosmo-knight entry. Standard Equipment is prose - whatever the knight''s
    normal identity would require, usually modest - naming no item the catalog
    could hold. So there is no `starting_money` and no `equipment_starting`,
    the same as the three classes of batch 8, and `--field-sources` has nothing
    to check on this class rather than having missed something.
  - THIS CLASS NEEDS NO `CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS` ENTRY. `withCorePools` in
    `js/compose.js` returns early for a class stating an `mdc_base`, and this
    one states 4D6x10+60. The rule that a class stating neither base needs an
    entry does not reach it.
  - Experience table transcribed from a 200 dpi render of printed 183, from the
    column headed `Cosmo-Knight`. All fifteen bands self-check: every band''s
    low is the previous band''s high plus one.
